# Component Usage Guide

This project uses a combination of Element Plus components and custom components to build the UI. Understanding how to use these components correctly is essential for maintaining consistency.

## Component Organization

- Global components are registered in [src/components/index.ts](mdc:src/components/index.ts)
- Each component has its own directory with a clear structure:
  - Main component file (e.g., `index.vue`)
  - Types or interfaces (if needed)
  - Subcomponents (if applicable)
  - Style files

## Key Component Categories

1. **Layout Components**
   - [ContentWrap](mdc:src/components/ContentWrap/) - Wrapper for page content with consistent padding/margins
   - [Card](mdc:src/components/Card/) - Content container with title and actions

2. **Data Input Components**
   - [Form](mdc:src/components/Form/) - Enhanced form components
   - [ColorInput](mdc:src/components/ColorInput/) - Color selector
   - [Crontab](mdc:src/components/Crontab/) - Cron expression editor

3. **Data Display Components**
   - [Table](mdc:src/components/Table/) - Enhanced data table with pagination
   - [Descriptions](mdc:src/components/Descriptions/) - Detail information display
   - [Echart](mdc:src/components/Echart/) - Chart components

4. **Special Components**
   - [Editor](mdc:src/components/Editor/) - Rich text editor
   - [Cropper](mdc:src/components/Cropper/) - Image cropping
   - [bpmnProcessDesigner](mdc:src/components/bpmnProcessDesigner/) - Business process designer

## Using Components

```vue
<template>
  <ContentWrap>
    <Form :schema="formSchema" @register="registerForm" />
    <Table :columns="columns" :data="tableData" />
  </ContentWrap>
</template>
```

When creating new components:
- Follow the existing component structure and naming conventions
- Use TypeScript for proper type definitions
- Leverage Element Plus components where possible rather than recreating functionality
- Document props, events, and slots for component reusability
